@startuml virtual_thread_capacity_overview
top to bottom direction
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 35
title Target-only Capacity: Boundary and Resource Ownership

' Source evidence:
' modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/Agent.java, VIRTUAL_THREAD_EXECUTOR and startExecution
' modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/loop/AgentLoop.java, consumeStream
' modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/tool/ToolExecutionPipeline.java, executeParallel
' modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/stream/EventStream.java, eventSink
' Observed behavior: agent and tool tasks already use virtual threads and blocking stream consumption.
' Architecture change: add deployment-level execution admission, byte budgets, and phase-local leases.
' Product constraint: callers see Session Events and Entries, never an execution resource or id.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #475569
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #475569
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #F8FAFC

actor "mate-service" as client

rectangle "CampusClaw HTTP Boundary" {
  component "Session Event API\nrequest-scoped SSE" as api
  component "Session Control API\nsteer, follow-up, abort" as control
  component "Auth and ResultBean Adapter" as auth
}

rectangle "Runtime Capacity Boundary" {
  component "Session Coordinator\none active execution" as session
  component "Capacity Manager\ncount and weighted bytes" as capacity
  queue "Bounded Admission\nitems, bytes, and time" as queue
  component "Execution Task\none virtual thread" as task
}

rectangle "Phase-Local Resources" {
  component "Model Lease" as model
  component "Tool Lease" as tool
  component "File Lease" as file
  component "Store Mailbox" as mailbox
  component "Bounded SSE Writer" as sse
}

database "RuntimeSessionStore\nSession and current-branch Entries" as store

client --> auth : independent HTTP request
auth --> api : authenticated event
auth --> control : authenticated control
api --> session : reserve idle Session
session --> capacity : acquire ExecutionLease
capacity --> queue : bounded wait
queue --> task : submit after lease
task --> model : model phase
task --> tool : tool phase
task --> file : file phase
task --> mailbox : durable Entry writes
mailbox --> store : commit before publish
task --> sse : live events
sse -[norank]-> api : text/event-stream
control -[norank]-> session : queue or cancel



legend bottom left
Retained capacity proposal; source evidence remains at the fixed 1957466 baseline.
Execution state and leases are internal; no public execution resource or ID.
Virtual threads are not pooled. Disconnect closes SSE projection only.
Accepted work continues; durable recovery reads Session Events.
endlegend
@enduml


@startuml execution_admission_and_lifecycle
' Source evidence:
' modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/Agent.java, startExecution
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/AgentSession.java, prompt and abort
' Observed behavior: one Agent execution is protected by a lock and runs asynchronously.
' Architecture change: add transactional acceptance and deployment-level capacity leases.
' Design reason: acceptance must survive an HTTP disconnect without exposing an execution resource.
title Target-only Admission and Execution Lifecycle
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam maxMessageSize 190
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  ParticipantBorderColor #64748B
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
}

actor "mate-service" as Client
boundary "Session Event API" as API
control "Session Coordinator" as Session
participant "Capacity Manager\nand bounded admission" as Capacity
database "RuntimeSessionStore" as Store
participant "Execution task\nvirtual thread" as Task
participant "SSE Writer" as SSE

== 1. Reserve capacity ==
Client -> API : Submit Session event
API -> API : Validate request and attachments
API -> Session : Reserve idle Session
break Session already running
  Session --> API : Conflict
  API --> Client : ResultBean error
end
Session -> Capacity : Acquire count and byte lease
Capacity --> Session : Lease or admission timeout
break No lease before deadline
  Session --> API : Admission rejected
  API --> Client : ResultBean error
end

== 2. Commit acceptance ==
Session -> Store : Commit User Entry, running state and fence
break Commit failed
  Store --> Session : Rolled back
  Session -> Capacity : Close lease once
  Session --> API : Rejected before acceptance
  API --> Client : ResultBean error
end
  Store --> Session : Committed Entry
  Session --> API : Accepted
  API --> Client : 200 text/event-stream
  API -> SSE : Publish accepted user.message
Session -> Task : Submit immutable execution context

== 3. Execute and release ==
Task -> Task : Model / Tool / File phases\nEach owns its resource lease
Task -> Store : Commit completed Entries
Store --> Task : Committed
Task -> SSE : Publish live and completed events
Task -> Store : Set idle; clear fence
Task -> Capacity : Close execution lease once
Task -> SSE : Idle and stream end
SSE -->> Client : Project available events

legend bottom left
This diagram belongs to the retained target-only capacity proposal.
An accepted execution survives disconnect; only SSE projection closes.
Admission groups two collaborators; it does not introduce a combined class.
endlegend
@enduml
@startuml bounded_sse_and_downstream
top to bottom direction
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 35
title Target-only Capacity: Bounded Channels and Downstream Isolation

' Source evidence:
' modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/loop/AgentLoop.java, consumeStream
' modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/stream/EventStream.java, unicast backpressure buffer
' Observed behavior: model events are consumed as a blocking stream with a buffered sink.
' Security hardening: every channel has explicit item and byte budgets and redacted failures.
' Design reason: one slow response must not retain provider, tool, file, or store capacity forever.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #475569
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #475569
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #F8FAFC

rectangle "Execution-Local Path" {
  component "Provider Reader\nconnect, first-token, idle timeout" as provider
  queue "Model Event Channel\nitems and bytes" as model_channel
  component "Agent Loop\nvirtual thread" as loop
  component "Delta Coalescer\n50 ms or 8 KiB" as coalescer
  queue "SSE Response Buffer\nitems and bytes" as buffer
  component "SSE Writer\nwrite timeout" as writer
}

rectangle "Isolated Downstream" {
  component "Tool Capacity\nglobal and per execution" as tools
  component "File Capacity\nbounded streaming" as files
  queue "Store Mailbox\nitems and bytes" as mailbox
}

database "RuntimeSessionStore\ndurable current-branch Entries" as store
actor "mate-service" as client

provider --> model_channel : structured increments
model_channel --> loop : backpressure-aware consume
loop --> tools : phase-local Tool Lease
loop --> files : phase-local File Lease
loop --> mailbox : completed Entry
mailbox --> store : durable commit
store -[norank]-> loop : commit acknowledged
loop --> coalescer : live delta and completion
coalescer --> buffer : ordered SSE event
buffer --> writer : bounded write
writer --> client : text/event-stream



legend bottom left
Every channel bounds both items and bytes. A stalled model phase is cancelled
at its deadline and releases its lease; it never buffers without a bound.
Disconnect closes projection only. No Last-Event-ID replay is provided.
Durable recovery reads Session Events.
endlegend
@enduml
